# Retro pixel icons for the target OS

The old machine being recovered (`target_os`: Aero taskbar, `LoginScreen`, `SystemExplorer`,
`NetExplorer`, `SectorRecover`, `OperatorNotes`, `PhotoViewer`, `Messenger`) uses a 110-piece
32x32 pixel-art icon set in `public/Old_Icons/`. Matching modern Linux-style SVGs live in
`public/new_icons/<name>.svg` (same keys as `RETRO_ICONS`) and are rendered with
`<ModernIcon name="..." />`, `modernAppIcon('...')`, or `<RetroIcon variant="modern" />`.
The host OS (`ModernDock`, `HostLoginScreen`, `news-browser`, `friend-chat`, `arcade`) keeps
its own SVG icons in `src/components/os/icons.tsx`.

## Rule

When adding or changing any app, file type, toolbar button, dialog, sidebar entry, status marker,
or other icon-like visual on the target OS:

1. Open `src/components/os/retroIcons.tsx` and search `RETRO_ICONS` by meaning (each key has a
   JSDoc describing the picture). Pick the closest match before drawing SVG, using emoji, or
   adding a new asset.
2. Render it with `<RetroIcon name="..." size={20|32|40|56|64} />` (pixel art) or
   `<ModernIcon name="..." />` / `<RetroIcon name="..." variant="modern" />` (vector).
   For app registry entries in `src/game/apps.ts` use `icon: retroAppIcon('...')` or
   `icon: modernAppIcon('...')`. For file kinds use `fileTypeIcon(type)`.
3. Keep sizes at the existing slots: 20 (title bar, taskbar, list rows), 32 (classic start, add-on
   rows), 40 (dialogs, modern start tiles), 56 (explorer tiles), 64 (desktop). The `.pixelated`
   class is applied automatically on the retro variant only.
4. Only if nothing fits, add a new PNG to `public/Old_Icons/` (and a matching SVG in
   `public/new_icons/`) with a descriptive kebab-case name and register it in `RETRO_ICONS`
   with a JSDoc line.

